%20hustle%20income/youtube-growth-course/companion/index.html">companion</a=
> and use the <strong>script</strong> experiment to estimate spoken duratio=
n from your word count and planned demonstration pauses. Change the speakin=
g rate rather than forcing your voice to match a number. The estimate is a =
planning model; your rehearsal is the final timing evidence. Once the scrip=
t is filmable, move to the filming chapter and collect the material your ex=
planation actually needs.</p>
<p><a id=3D"chapter-04-section-22"></a></p>
<h3>Focused learning resources</h3>
<p>YouTube's <a href=3D"https://support.google.com/youtube/answer/9314415">=
audience-retention guidance</a> explains the platform's retention report; u=
se the next chapter's production process to create the footage, then the gr=
owth chapter to interpret the results. Platform reporting is evidence about=
 viewing behavior, not a substitute for judging whether the explanation is =
true and understandable.</p>
<p>For the teaching craft, study your own strongest technical article as an=
 adaptation exercise: keep its central example, convert paragraphs into spo=
ken sentences, and replace each abstract paragraph with a concrete screen a=
ction or diagram where possible. This uses work you understand and can veri=
fy, which is a better starting point than asking an assistant to invent an =
impressive topic outside your experience.</p>
<p>The next chapter turns this document into clean recordings. You now know=
 what the camera, microphone, screen capture, and editor must communicate; =
that makes equipment choices much easier to evaluate.</p>
